    <h2 class="lesson-heading">Error handling</h2>

    <p>
      The course defines four error categories. Add a <code>try/catch</code> in
      <code>runSpecialist</code> that handles each:
    </p>

    <CodeBlock lang="typescript" label="supervisor.service.ts — runSpecialist" code={`
try {
  // ... agent loop
} catch (err) {
  if (err.status === 429) {
    // Transient: rate limit — retry with exponential backoff
    throw new ServiceUnavailableException('Rate limit hit, please retry');
  }
  if (err.status === 401) {
    // Permanent: bad API key — log and fail loudly
    throw new InternalServerErrorException('Agent configuration error');
  }
  // Default: log with context, return graceful message
  console.error({ specialist: key, message, err });
  return 'I ran into a problem handling your request. A human agent will follow up.';
}
    `} />

    <LessonCallout variant="warn" title="Don't swallow errors silently">
      <p>
        A catch-all that logs and continues lets the agent "work" while producing wrong results.
        Be explicit: transient errors retry, permanent errors fail loudly, partial errors degrade gracefully.
      </p>
    </LessonCallout>

