    <h2 class="lesson-heading">§1.4 — The Autonomy Spectrum</h2>

    <p>
      Your SupportDesk API sits at the boundary between agentic workflow and autonomous agent.
      Understanding where your system lives on this spectrum — and why — is the first design
      decision for every agent project.
    </p>

    <LessonDiagram definition={`
flowchart LR
  A["Agentic Workflow\nEngineers define\nthe graph structure"]:::workflow
  B["Hybrid\nFixed graph +\nautonomous steps"]:::hybrid
  C["Autonomous Agent\nAgent decides\nits own steps"]:::auto

  A -->|"Add conditional edges"| B
  B -->|"Agent creates steps dynamically"| C

  note1["Predictable\nAuditable\nLow risk"]:::note
  note2["Flexible\nCreative\nHigher risk"]:::note

  A -.-> note1
  C -.-> note2

  classDef workflow fill:#dbeafe,color:#1e3a8a,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
  classDef hybrid   fill:#ede9fe,color:#4c1d95,stroke:#7c3aed,stroke-width:2px
  classDef auto     fill:#dcfce7,color:#14532d,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef note     fill:#f8fafc,color:#64748b,stroke:#e2e8f0,stroke-width:1px,font-style:italic
    `} />

    <h3 class="lesson-heading">The six autonomy levels</h3>

    <p>
      The three-point spectrum above maps to six concrete implementation levels.
      The deep dive references these by number — they give you a precise vocabulary
      for design discussions, threat modelling, and deciding when to graduate a system
      to the next level.
    </p>

    <LessonDiagram definition={`
flowchart LR
  L1["1 · Notify\nLLM text only\nno tools"]:::low
  L2["2 · Classify\nStructured output\nhuman or code acts"]:::low
  L3["3 · Chain\nFixed LLM sequence\nengineers define steps"]:::mid
  L4["4 · Route\nLLM picks path\nfixed options only"]:::mid
  L5["5 · Orchestrate\nLLM navigates\nstate machine"]:::high
  L6["6 · Automate\nAgent owns\nits own steps"]:::high

  L1 --> L2 --> L3 --> L4 --> L5 --> L6

  classDef low  fill:#dbeafe,color:#1e3a8a,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
  classDef mid  fill:#ede9fe,color:#4c1d95,stroke:#7c3aed,stroke-width:2px
  classDef high fill:#dcfce7,color:#14532d,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    `} />

